{# pdoc's sidebar heading for a module's members is "API Documentation".

   In this project "the API" is the web API at numberdb.org/api -- a different
   thing with its own reference, linked from the same help page. A reader who
   arrives at the package reference looking for the web API and finds a heading
   promising it has been sent to the wrong document by the document itself.

   "Contents" is what the list under it actually is. #}
{% extends "default/module.html.jinja2" %}

{% block nav_members %}
    {% if module.members %}
        <h2>Contents</h2>
        {{ nav_members(module.members.values()) }}
    {% endif %}
{% endblock %}
